LIE optionally links the system Zstandard C library for lossless checkpoints.
No library implementation is vendored. The private Strix Point build capsule
may carry the matching system development headers and license, with SHA-256
identities, when the pinned runtime image lacks those headers. Zstandard is
dual licensed; LIE uses it under the BSD-3-Clause option. Preserve the package
license when distributing.
Upstream: https://github.com/facebook/zstd
License: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/blob/dev/LICENSE
Local validation uses system 1.5.7 and static-context advanced APIs exported by
that matched header/library: estimateCCtxSize, estimateDCtxSize,
initStaticCCtx/DCtx, compressCCtx and decompressDCtx. Context/workspace memory
is allocated by LIE and included in admission. The byte-plane permutation,
framing, state lifetime and retention policy are independently written MIT C17.
